# Cursor Rules

## Safety Rules

### Process Management
- **NEVER use `pkill -f main`** - This command will kill ALL programs/processes that contain "main" in their name or command line, which is extremely dangerous and can affect other important system processes.
- Always use more specific process identification when killing processes:
  - Use specific process names or PIDs
  - Use `ps aux | grep <specific_name>` to identify the exact process first
  - Use full program paths or more precise matching patterns
  - Use `kill <PID>` to target specific processes

## Development Guidelines

### Go Development
- This is a Go-based microservices project using distributed architecture
- Follow Go best practices and conventions
- Apply code changes automatically when requested

### Project Context
- This is a daily brief system with GitLab, Feishu, and AI integrations
- Always consider the impact of changes on the distributed system architecture 